-- Pass 100 §15 — `goto` is a load-bearing absence. Failure is the assertion.
--
-- Jumping to a label is the shape §13 replaces with a dispatch table:
-- `next(state)(event) = handler`, where exhaustiveness and the diagram come
-- free. Measured zero users over the 767 tracked `.duo` files, 2026-08-08,
-- with `"…"` and `[[ … ]]` bodies both stripped.
--
-- Its twin `pass100_goto_retired.lua` is the same program in Lua and must
-- still compile. That pair IS the dialect split — one construct, two
-- extensions, two answers — and the `.lua` half is the load-bearing one: it
-- proves the construct was gated on the dialect rather than removed from the
-- compiler.
--
-- The pattern this row asserts is the REPAIR ("dispatch table"), not the
-- refusal line, because a diagnostic that only says no makes the corpus
-- unmigratable.

main(): i64
    i = 0
    while i < 3
        i = i + 1
        goto skip
        print(i)
        ::skip::
